  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of the member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CEACR Observation on C 100- Jordan

&quot;The Committee notes with satisfaction that section 2 of the Labour Code (Amendments) Act No. 14, 2019, defines non-discrimination in relation to wages as the application of the principle of equal remuneration for work of equal value regardless of gender.&quot;
 The Office provided advocacy as well as advice and assistance in relation to efforts to bring about legislative change aimed at pay equity and the application of the principle of equal pay for work of equal value, in the context of its broader efforts aimed at gender equality and a stronger labour force participation of women in Jordan. To achieve these goals, the Office worked in close collaboration with the social partners as well as with other partners from civil society.</narrative>
   </description>
